# ==================================================================================================
# Every storage tier with both signs
# DecimalCastOperation is a template: each of int16, int32, int64 and int128 storage, for positive and for negative
# values, is a separate instantiation with its own overflow limits. The same 12 input shapes (padding, rounding, surplus
# decimals beyond the storage type, exponent 0 / positive / negative, overflow after scaling or by exponent) are run for
# DECIMAL(4,2), (9,4), (18,9) and (38,19) - the widest type of each tier, so the storage type is exactly full - with and
# without a minus sign, so that no tier or sign is left out for any branch.
# ==================================================================================================

